# 🌍 Two-Phase Commit (2PC) - The Transaction That Says "Sab Commit Karo Ya Sab Cancel!" 🤝

> **One Line Definition**
>
> **Two-Phase Commit (2PC)** ek distributed transaction protocol hai jo ensure karta hai ki agar transaction multiple databases/partitions par chal raha hai to **ya to sab commit hoga ya fir sab rollback hoga.**
>
> 🎯 **All or Nothing.**
>
> Atomicity across multiple machines.

---

# 🤔 Pehle Problem Samjho

Imagine tumhare paas sirf **1 database** hai.

User ₹100 transfer karta hai.

```
A -= 100
B += 100
```

Simple.

Database ACID maintain kar lega.

---

## Lekin Distributed System me?

Suppose...

```
User A -> Database 1
User B -> Database 2
```

Ab transfer karna hai.

```
DB1:
A = A -100

DB2:
B = B +100
```

Question👇

Agar DB1 ne commit kar diya...

Aur DB2 crash ho gaya...

To?

```
A ke account se paise chale gaye ❌

B ko paise mile hi nahi ❌
```

Money Gayab 😭

Ye Atomicity toot gayi.

Isi problem ko solve karta hai...

